From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivo Nunes <ivo@nunes.uk>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 11:26:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Rendering: keep a directional shadow's far splits for a few
 frames

rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/cache_far_splits (on by
default) draws the third of four splits every other frame and the fourth
every fourth frame (the second of two every other frame), on frames of their
own, instead of all of them every frame. A kept split is drawn with 5% more
room and drawn again at once when the camera leaves it, the light turns more
than half a degree, the shadow's size or split count changes, another
view draws over the atlas, or the scenario shifts (scenario_shift()). Each drawn split clears its own part of the atlas
rather than the whole atlas being cleared first.

In a large city scene this drew a third fewer shadow primitives and saved
about 8% of the GPU's frame.
---
 godot/doc/classes/ProjectSettings.xml         |  3 +
 .../drivers/gles3/rasterizer_scene_gles3.cpp  |  6 ++
 godot/drivers/gles3/storage/light_storage.cpp | 17 ++---
 .../render_forward_clustered.cpp              |  6 +-
 .../forward_mobile/render_forward_mobile.cpp  |  6 +-
 .../servers/rendering/renderer_scene_cull.cpp | 70 ++++++++++++++++++-
 godot/servers/rendering/renderer_scene_cull.h | 31 +++++++-
 7 files changed, 119 insertions(+), 20 deletions(-)

diff --git a/godot/doc/classes/ProjectSettings.xml b/godot/doc/classes/ProjectSettings.xml
index d99a5d94..1c295f85 100644
--- a/godot/doc/classes/ProjectSettings.xml
+++ b/godot/doc/classes/ProjectSettings.xml
@@ -3193,6 +3193,9 @@
 		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/16_bits" type="bool" setter="" getter="" default="true">
 			Use 16 bits for the directional shadow depth map. Enabling this results in shadows having less precision and may result in shadow acne, but can lead to performance improvements on some devices.
 		</member>
+		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/cache_far_splits" type="bool" setter="" getter="" default="true">
+			If [code]true[/code], the farthest splits of a [DirectionalLight3D]'s shadow are drawn every few frames instead of every frame, which saves much of the shadow's cost in large scenes. With [constant DirectionalLight3D.SHADOW_PARALLEL_4_SPLITS], the third split is drawn every other frame and the fourth every fourth frame; with [constant DirectionalLight3D.SHADOW_PARALLEL_2_SPLITS], the second split every other frame. A kept split is drawn again at once when the camera moves out of what it covers, the light turns, or another viewport draws the shadow. Moving objects' shadows in the far splits follow a frame or a few behind. Read when the project starts.
+		</member>
 		<member name="rendering/lights_and_shadows/directional_shadow/size" type="int" setter="" getter="" default="4096">
 			The directional shadow's size in pixels. Higher values will result in sharper shadows, at the cost of performance. The value is rounded up to the nearest power of 2.
 		</member>
